{"id": "clm:d9a4b39af50e64b3d579ab90f6cd0cd34ab9691478a9935fcd2276db27bf6e3a", "type": "statement", "text": "Lo, Mamaysky and Wang (2000) report incremental information in several technical indicators when comparing conditional and unconditional daily US stock return distributions. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://web.mit.edu/wangj/www/pap/LoMamayskyWang00.pdf", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Causal price-action geometry"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b71e1cfa772b6e98a295a96409560d638227ecc1ae9528a993fa6d5ae896e114", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4a89efa470115401ecee432e192c6eee1f07faadf3286524cceb7a0a95a513b3", "ev:b01002d38c0415c07b6d6ab1024de9466ecd25d04ebff8791fa4aa1b6d10f807", "ev:bf9294c97c60d9f9a60dd834d20cf5ed6f5a7da0d96c4cfd6340e033aa2da007"]}
